From cd9a4372d990cf96d7d40b911524ebfe0b454479 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:53:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sensors: one tab per category in the details popover

The details popover stacked every category (CPU, GPU, storage, system, per-core
usage, memory, disks) in one tall scrolling column. On a 16 inch panel it
reached the dock and the lists were cut at six rows.

Group the rows into tabs with Singularity.Widgets.SegmentedControl driving a
Gtk.Stack: CPU (temperatures and clocks), Processor (per-core usage), Memory &
Storage (sensors, RAM, swap, volumes, activity) and Hardware (GPU, NPU, VPU,
system, board, network). Empty tabs are left out and the selected tab is kept
across the periodic refresh. Grouped/Ungrouped still applies inside every tab
and the column count from the logical width is unchanged; ungrouped CPU
temperatures and clocks are separate sections so they fill both columns. The
per-group row cap goes from 6 to 12 so a 12-core CPU is shown in full. The
height cap stays as a safety net: monitor height minus the chip's bottom edge,
the dock (dock-icon-size plus padding) and a gap, never below 240 px.
